---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../site.config';
---

<Base
  title="Newsletter signup help"
  description="Help with newsletter signup, connection problems, and confirmation emails, plus an RSS alternative."
  noindex
>
  <div class="container narrow section">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Newsletter signup help</p><h1>
        Take a moment, then try again.
      </h1><p>
        A connection or provider problem can get in the way. This page does not
        establish whether a signup request succeeded.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Check your connection and email address</h2><p>
        If you are offline, reconnect before trying again. Use a complete email
        address, such as name@example.com, and check it for typing mistakes.
      </p>
      <h2>Follow the email provider's instructions</h2><p>
        The signup form sends your request directly to the email provider. If
        its page shows an error or extra steps, follow those instructions. If
        the provider is unavailable, wait and try again later.
      </p>
      <p>
        We cannot check a subscription from this page. Do not send private
        health information through a signup field.
      </p>
      <h2>Look for a confirmation email</h2><p>
        Check your inbox and spam or junk folder. A request is not an active
        subscription until you complete the provider's confirmation process. <a
          href="/newsletter/confirm/">Read the confirmation guidance</a
        >.
      </p>
      {
        site.newsletter.action ? (
          <p>
            <a class="button" href="/newsletter/#newsletter-signup">
              Try signup again
            </a>
          </p>
        ) : (
          <div class="callout">
            <>
              <h2>The newsletter is coming soon.</h2>
              <p>
                Signup is not connected in this version of the site. You can
                check the <a href="/newsletter/">newsletter page</a> for
                availability.
              </p>
            </>
          </div>
        )
      }
      <h2>Another way to follow along</h2><p>
        The <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a> works with your preferred feed reader
        and does not ask for an email address. Or <a href="/blog/"
          >explore the articles</a
        > whenever you like.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
